<title>FRANCE: Workers to occupy insolvent French TV factory.</title>
<headline>Workers to occupy insolvent French TV factory.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Employees of an insolvent television set maker in eastern France voted on Wednesday to occupy the firm's factory beginning on May 6 in protest at plans to lay off 165 workers.</p>
<p>Union officials said that 185 of set-maker Gooding's 365 employees had voted in favour of occupying the plant in Creutzwald, near France's border with Germany, while 162 had voted against the plan.</p>
<p>The planned layoffs are part of a court-approved plan for the plant, now under judicial administration, to be taken over by French electronics firm COFIDUR on May 12.</p>
<p>After that date, sets would be made under the Continental Edison brand name.</p>
<p>Gooding officials have invited all employees to a meeting on Monday afternoon in an apparent effort to head off any move to occupy the plant.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
